 "about": "What each leveling route was in Grimoire 1.0.6 as released (data/guide.json of November 15, 2026, 02:17 EST, commit 7056444): its hours, its visits (a \"Go to\" and the work done there), its \"Go to\" steps, its changes of continent (`sails`: those not made by the class’s own teleport), its short visits (`thin`: fewer than three quests handed in), its stays on a continent that hand in fewer than three quests (`hops`), its \"kill to the next level\" steps, the levels they add up to (`ground`), the longest run of levels in a row ground for more than half (`run`), the levels ground in stretches of a level or more in a row (`row`: grind steps at levels that follow each other, each longer than a third of its level, adding up to a level or more), as lib/route-bar.mjs counts them, and the rule of lib/guide.mjs the route was worked out by then (`rule`; the Skyborne routes continue another route and have none). lib/guide.mjs holds every rule to these (the gate in buildGuide): no more hours, fewer levels ground, no more levels ground in a row unless the route grinds as much less in all (`ground` and `row` together: no more), and inside `bar`: at most `thin` more short visits (counted from the released median, `median.thin`, for a route under it) and one more for every level the route no longer grinds, and never over `continentsMost` changes of continent, the class’s own teleports aside (or as many as here), unless the route is both faster and grinds less than here. A route no rule passes for is worked out by its `rule`, which gives the released route again. check-routes.mjs holds every route to the same.",
